# packages/db/.env.example
# Copy this file to packages/db/.env and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env — it is gitignored.

# ── Neon / Vercel Postgres ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# DATABASE_URL  – POOLED connection string (PgBouncer, used by Prisma Client at
#                 runtime on serverless/Vercel). Hostname contains "-pooler".
#                 e.g. ep-xxx-pooler.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech
#
# DIRECT_URL    – DIRECT (non-pooled) connection string (used by Prisma Migrate
#                 and Prisma Studio so they bypass the pooler). No "-pooler".
#                 e.g. ep-xxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech
#
# In the Neon console both URLs are shown on the "Connection Details" page.
# In local dev you can set both to the same direct URL.
#
# !! PowerShell warning !!
# Do NOT paste these into the terminal — the & in query params will be
# interpreted as a background operator. Always edit .env with a text editor:
#   notepad packages/db/.env
# or copy this file and fill in values without touching the shell.
#
# ── Vercel env vars ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# In the Vercel dashboard add both vars under Settings > Environment Variables.
# Paste the raw URL (no surrounding quotes) into the value field.
# Vercel quotes/escapes values for you — do NOT double-quote them there.

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DATABASE?channel_binding=require&sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DATABASE?sslmode=require"
